ESP32 OLED Display – Reflection

This project introduced me to using an OLED display with the ESP32 through the I2C communication protocol. I learned how to wire the display correctly, install the required graphics libraries, initialize the display, and print text to the screen. Unlike serial output, the OLED provides a visual interface that makes embedded projects much more user-friendly.

One of the most valuable lessons was understanding how peripherals communicate over I2C and how software libraries simplify working with display hardware. I also gained experience troubleshooting wiring connections, library installation, and display initialization issues.

Completing this project strengthened my understanding of embedded systems and prepared me for more advanced projects that combine displays with sensors, Wi-Fi, and real-time data. Going forward, I plan to use OLED displays in IoT dashboards, environmental monitoring systems, robotics projects, and smart home applications.

Overall, this project improved my hardware integration, debugging, and programming skills while moving me another step closer to becoming an embedded systems engineer.
